# Modelfile.ornith-9b-ad — Ornith 1.5 9B dynamic-quant variant (AD).
#
# Ornith-1.5-9B with the AtomicChat/DeepReinforce "AD" static-sparse
# (Q8_0 experts layering) requantisation: Ornith-1.5-9B-AD-Q8_0-Q6_K.
# Slightly higher quality than the stock Q6_K at the cost of ~1.5 GB and
# a couple fewer tok/s. Measured on the reference box: ~35.6 gen tok/s
# @ 8K → ~35.6 @ 64K (0.0 % drop), still flat but ~6 % slower than the
# stock Q6_K primary.
#
# Use this when the bottleneck is output quality rather than latency on
# a context that is close to the model's comfort limit. The stock Q6_K
# (`Modelfile.ornith-9b`) remains the default primary.
#
# Manual GGUF drop: place the GGUF in /bulk/models/ first.
#
#   ollama create ornith-9b-ad -f config/ollama/Modelfile.ornith-9b-ad

FROM /bulk/models/Ornith-1.5-9B-AD-Q8_0-Q6_K.gguf

SYSTEM """$(cat config/ollama/PROMPT.coding.md)"""

PARAMETER temperature        0.2
PARAMETER top_p              0.95
PARAMETER top_k              40
PARAMETER repeat_penalty     1.05
PARAMETER num_ctx            65536

# keep_alive is server-side (OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=10m), not a Modelfile PARAMETER.
